This is needed (in both SSOS and SSP) in order to solve https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/141.

Last week, I talked to Joe about that bug and he thought that we'd already supplied this information, because the header `HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR` should be included in `session$request` (see test app at the bottom). However, when we actually tried it, he realized that that header is actually not being passed through because, in the call to `httpProxy.createProxyServer`, the option `xfwd` is not set. 
See https://github.com/nodejitsu/node-http-proxy#options. 
(I'd think the default would be `true`, but maybe that's not happening?)

I think the place to do it is here: 
https://github.com/rstudio/shiny-server/blob/master/lib/proxy/http.js#L236-L238

(I think that's the only place, but I'm not sure)

As we figured it out, Joe suggested that it may also be a good idea to make sure there's no other relevant options that we're not setting (since at least he thought we were passing the `HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR` when we weren't).

Another detail: it's important to make sure that `HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR` is present in the server (i.e. inside `session$request`) and not only in the ui (i.e. inside the `req` arg which is present if the UI is a function with that argument). 

Here's the test app (in SSOS and SSP, the `HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR` should be present, but it's not). It prints out both the ui's `req` elements and the server's `session$request` elements. (Finally, it also checks if `HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR` is present in the server and prints it out, otherwise defaulting to `REMOTE_ADDR` -- this last bit is basically what we should suggest for  https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/141 once this is fixed.)

<details>
  <summary>app.R</font></summary>

```r
library(shiny)

ui_xfwd <- NULL

ui <- function(req) {
  if ("HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR" %in% ls(req)) ui_xfwd <<- req[["HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR"]]
  fluidPage(
    h3("UI req"),
    paste(ls(req), collapse = " "),
    h3("server session$request"),
    textOutput("request"),
    h3("result"),
    uiOutput("result")
  )
}

server <- function(input, output, session) {
  output$request <- renderText({
    paste(ls(session$request), collapse = " ")
  })
  
  output$result <- renderUI({
    if ("HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR" %in% ls(session$request)) {
      div(
        p("HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR header present in server:"),
        p(session$request[["HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR"]])
      )
    } else if (!is.null(ui_xfwd)) {
      div(
        p("HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR header present in UI:"),
        p(ui_xfwd)
      )
    } else {
      div(
        p("HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR header not present in UI or server; here's the REMOTE_ADDR:"),
        p(session$request[["REMOTE_ADDR"]])
      )
    }
  })
}

shinyApp(ui, server)
```

